## Log Analysis Tips

### Key Log Patterns to Watch
- `[KEYBINDINGS]`: Input system events
- `[GAME_LOOP]`: Game loop updates
- `[RENDERING]`: Canvas and drawing operations
- `[THRUSTER]`: Thruster-specific debug info
- `[NETWORK]`: WebSocket and network events
- `[SHIP]`: Ship behavior and laser firing
- `[MOUSE]`: Mouse input handling
- `[GAME_CONTROLLER]`: Game initialization and lifecycle
- `[LASER]`: Laser creation and management
- `[COLLISION]`: Collision detection events

### Filtering Logs for Specific Issues
```bash
# Movement debugging
grep -E "shipPosition|shipAngle|thrusting" logs/client.log

# Rendering debugging  
grep -E "Drawing|Rendering|Canvas" logs/client.log

# Input debugging
grep -E "KeyDown|KeyUp|thrust|Mouse" logs/client.log

# Laser communication debugging
grep -E "shoot|laser|playerShoot|sendShootEvent" logs/client.log
grep -E "shoot|laser|playerShoot|DEBUG.*shoot" logs/server.log

# Network debugging
grep -E "WebSocket|connection|message" logs/client.log
grep -E "Player connected|Player disconnected" logs/server.log

# Game initialization debugging
grep -E "startGame|initializeListeners|Game area loaded" logs/client.log

# Collision debugging
grep -E "collision|hit|damage|split" logs/client.log
grep -E "collision|hit|damage|split" logs/server.log
```

